    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_6",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Carlo Rovelli (born 3 May 1956) is an Italian theoretical physicist and writer who has worked in Italy, the United States and since 2000, in France. His work is mainly in the field of quantum gravity, where he is among the founders of the loop quantum gravity theory. He has also worked in the history and philosophy of science. He collaborates regularly with several Italian newspapers, in particular the cultural supplements of \"Il Corriere della Sera\", \"Il Sole 24 Ore\" and \"La Repubblica\".",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999976094018,
