      "node_id": "kg_doc_2",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Aldo Pontremoli (] ; 19 January 1896 – 25 May 1928) was an Italian physicist who held a chair of theoretical physics at the University of Milan from 1926 and who founded and directed the Institute of Advanced Physics at the University of Milan from 1924 until his disappearance and presumed death in May 1928. Pontremoli was one of the six men who disappeared with the airborne envelope of the airship \"Italia\" after it had crashed on the Arctic ice on 25 May 1928.",
